    "title": "Business owner challenges Pensacola ordinance after misdemeanor warning at MLK Plaza - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Melanie Levi ,\n8 hours ago PENSACOLA, Fla. -- Dr. Martin Luther King Jr. Plaza is a walkable median that sits between Chase and Gregory streets downtown. The city of Pensacola considers it a park, and like all city parks, it closes to the public at sunset, but many locals say it's nothing more than just a concrete island and should stay open. Read full article\nRead in NewsBreak",
